WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:06.260
[DETECTIVE] WHO DID THIS?

00:00:07.020 --> 00:00:12.720
It certainly wasn't me. No, no. Somebody, NOT ME, must have moved it between the time

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:16.420
I was the last person alone with the body in the room and then stepped out for a few minutes

00:00:16.420 --> 00:00:19.180
to take care of some personal business that you don't need to know about!

00:00:19.840 --> 00:00:21.980
Could have been anybody... except me.

00:00:22.860 --> 00:00:24.280
[BUTLER] What the hell happened here?

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.552
[DETECTIVE] The body's been moved.

00:00:25.560 --> 00:00:26.380
[BUTLER] On its own?

00:00:26.380 --> 00:00:32.580
[DETECTIVE] No, of course not. Unless it did, in which case we've got way bigger problems than a simple murder.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.100
[CHEF] What the hell happened here?

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.160
[BUTLER] The body's moved.

00:00:35.160 --> 00:00:35.940
[CHEF] On its own?

00:00:35.940 --> 00:00:39.940
[DETECTIVE] We haven't quite ruled that out just yet, but let's not forget we've got a murderer.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:41.380
[COLONEL] Bully!

00:00:41.380 --> 00:00:45.820
Quite a storm out there, eh, chaps? What are you doing huddled in here in fear?

00:00:46.160 --> 00:00:47.600
[CHEF] We have a zombie problem.

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:52.400
[COLONEL] Ah, Homo necrosis! The MOST dangerous game.

00:00:52.420 --> 00:00:56.940
Well, if someone needs to put the old lad down again, I'm well up for the privilege.

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.500
[DETECTIVE] What do you mean by "again", and what do you mean by "privilege"?

00:01:00.500 --> 00:01:02.120
[COLONEL] I'm just saying, I've got plenty of...

00:01:03.129 --> 00:01:05.100
e-experience on the matter.

00:01:05.100 --> 00:01:05.920
[CHEF] So do I.

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:08.160
[DETECTIVE] Yeah, that just raises more questions.

00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:12.500
[COLONEL] Well, I'm off to the grounds to see if I can catch a whiff of the old bag of bones, eh?

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:15.140
[BUTLER] Wait, weren't you and Mark the same age?

00:01:15.380 --> 00:01:17.260
[COLONEL's maniacal laugh ends with a cough]

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.840
[DETECTIVE] All right, I don't trust him. Then again, I don't trust anyone.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:25.400
Alright, lock this place down. Secure the front gate.

00:01:25.409 --> 00:01:28.828
I don't want anyone in or out of this place until we get to the bottom of this.

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:32.200
[BUTLER] Locks won't keep people from getting out, sir.

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:34.100
[CHEF] Locks won't, but Chef will.

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:40.240
[DETECTIVE] Look, you're a real smart son of a bitch. Handsome, too. Beautiful, even.

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.020
BUT, we don't have time for this.

00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:46.680
I think we forgot the most important question of all during our arousing game of whodunit.

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:48.420
Why?

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:50.060
Why?

00:01:51.300 --> 00:01:53.300
Come, walk with me.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:57.400
Why did he invite us all here? Why tonight?

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.960
He said we were celebrating something, but he never specified what.

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:05.280
It's almost as if this whole shindig of a hootenanny was just a ruse.

00:02:05.520 --> 00:02:13.340
Mark was my friend: had been for years. But then he went quiet. I knew something was wrong, I just never figured out what.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:15.740
Now I guess I never will.

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:21.020
Look, I'm gonna level with you; you're my new partner. I've been working with him for years.

00:02:21.880 --> 00:02:26.900
Now I've been doing this for a long time, and I know something is wrong. There is a murderer—

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:28.680
[thunder and lightning]

00:02:28.680 --> 00:02:30.200
—here amongst us, and we need to find him.

00:02:31.480 --> 00:02:38.880
Now you look like a trustworthy...somebody. I know we just met, but I am an excellent judge of character.

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:41.860
Excellent like a fox.

00:02:42.840 --> 00:02:49.360
I smiled and fed them a line of bullshit. The truth was, I couldn't trust them any more than the other skuzz around here.

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:55.460
But like my late partner once said right before he died, best to keep your enemies close. Wink wink.

00:02:55.900 --> 00:02:59.060
You don't look like you have a reason to kill him. And if you do...

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:02.040
[laughs]

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:05.940
Best to keep your enemies close, eh? Wink wink.

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:09.840
So, the real question we should be asking is:

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:12.560
Who stood to gain the most from Mark's death?

00:03:12.560 --> 00:03:20.420
Now, in my thorough analysis of the corpse's anal cavity, I discovered that in addition to being stabbed 37 times,

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:25.500
he was also poisoned, beaten, strangled, drowned, and shot, in that order.

00:03:25.500 --> 00:03:32.040
Now, if you ask me, that's a lot of trouble to go through to knock off one guy, and it sure as shit is no accident.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:39.360
No. No, my friend. There's gonna be no simple candlestick-in-the-library solution to this whole...puzzle.

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:47.320
So, we're gonna have to do the detective-ly thing and go through the victim's most private and personal possessions.

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.440
Well, after you.

00:04:01.080 --> 00:04:08.400
[sighs] Looks rough, but I don't think he was killed here. Take a look around, see if you find anything, but BE CAREFUL.

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.720
I've lost three partners before to bedroom booby traps.

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.680
Make sure you don't tamper with any evidence!

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.060
Lemme know if you find anything.

00:04:27.380 --> 00:04:28.460
You find a clue?

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:32.780
[COLONEL] You're quite on the case, aren't you?

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:37.380
Say, detective? May I borrow your friend here?

00:04:37.540 --> 00:04:38.680
[DETECTIVE] Yeah, sure.

00:04:38.680 --> 00:04:41.720
Don't worry, partner, I'll handle it from here.

00:04:41.820 --> 00:04:42.800
[COLONEL] Bully.

00:04:43.400 --> 00:04:48.120
Take a walk with me. I thought that it was about time that we got to...

00:04:48.460 --> 00:04:50.180
KNOW each other.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:54.520
Someplace far, far away from the prying eyes of, uh...

00:04:54.720 --> 00:04:56.720
anyone else.

00:04:57.180 --> 00:04:58.840
Come with me.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:05.200
Now correct me if I'm wrong, but...you and the Mayor know each other, right?

00:05:05.640 --> 00:05:10.740
He's a good man, that one. We've been fast friends for as long as I can remember.

00:05:11.420 --> 00:05:14.940
Now there came a time when I could have said the same thing about Mark, but..

00:05:16.760 --> 00:05:22.520
Well, best not to speak ill of the dead. Oh! The pool hasn't aged a day!

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:25.960
GERONIMO!

00:05:27.700 --> 00:05:29.080
[MAYOR] Have you seen the Colonel?

00:05:31.180 --> 00:05:33.180
I thought I heard him.

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:37.340
I need to speak with him. I may have been a little short at our last encounter.

00:05:38.460 --> 00:05:40.220
Well, if you do see him, let me know.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:43.420
[COLONEL] BULLY!

00:05:44.800 --> 00:05:49.440
[COLONEL] Oh, life needs a bit of madness, eh, chap? Now, what were we talking about?

00:05:50.080 --> 00:05:52.480
Oh, yes! The grisly business inside.

00:05:53.060 --> 00:05:58.800
Well, I'm sure I'm not the first to say that our host had a great deal of enemies as of late.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:07.200
My prying eye might suspect that the people who worked for him might have reason to stab him in the back.

00:06:08.080 --> 00:06:11.340
God knows he's a tough son of a bitch to work for.

00:06:12.280 --> 00:06:15.040
Oh, the old golf course! I-I'll fetch my clubs.

00:06:19.840 --> 00:06:20.760
[MAYOR] Colonel?

00:06:21.300 --> 00:06:25.000
Damn, I thought I heard him. No matter. Would you accompany me?

00:06:25.000 --> 00:06:30.180
There's something that I would...very much like to discuss with you. Now, I know you've been assisting our...

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:33.600
intrepid detective with his investigation, but...

00:06:34.120 --> 00:06:36.580
I have to bring some concerns of mine to the forefront.

00:06:37.320 --> 00:06:43.140
If we look at this situation logically, we can only assume that the killer who struck down our dear friend Mark

00:06:43.440 --> 00:06:45.440
was with us last night.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.740
And while I would stake my life on the innocence of the Colonel or yourself,

00:06:51.660 --> 00:06:55.680
can we really say the same of our beloved detective?

00:06:57.040 --> 00:06:59.040
Or worse yet,

00:06:59.860 --> 00:07:05.440
Mayhaps our counting skills aren't as good as we assume them to be. And mayhaps...

00:07:06.660 --> 00:07:11.940
in the shadows of this manor, unseen to any of us, lay hidden...

00:07:13.600 --> 00:07:14.300
...a murderer.

00:07:14.300 --> 00:07:14.800
[Thunder and lightning]

00:07:14.800 --> 00:07:15.800
[Gunshot]

00:07:21.400 --> 00:07:24.440
[DETECTIVE] I don't know what you're playing at but you better lower your weapon, you murderer!

00:07:24.440 --> 00:07:28.980
[COLONEL] I bloody well won't, you're the one that assaulted me! For all I know, you could be the murderer!

00:07:28.980 --> 00:07:30.100
[CHEF] What the fu-Ooh!

00:07:30.100 --> 00:07:31.980
[DETECTIVE] Last chance, drop your weapon!

00:07:32.140 --> 00:07:33.740
[BUTLER] Master's prized vase...

00:07:33.740 --> 00:07:38.240
[MAYOR] Everyone, please! I know we're all on edge, but can't we resolve this amicably?

00:07:38.240 --> 00:07:40.580
[DETECTIVE] On edge?! This PSYCHO tried to SHOOT ME!

00:07:40.580 --> 00:07:44.200
[COLONEL] That's a bold-faced lie! I was merely doing some light target practice!

00:07:44.360 --> 00:07:45.360
[BUTLER] Inside?!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:49.680
[COLONEL] Well, yes, I couldn't go on the grounds now with that bloody chef in my way, could I?

00:07:49.680 --> 00:07:52.260
[CHEF] You're damn right! You should've remembered that, Private!

00:07:52.260 --> 00:07:54.460
Besides, you're not my boss anymore!

00:07:54.460 --> 00:07:55.940
[COLONEL] It's "Colonel" now.

00:07:55.940 --> 00:08:01.600
[DETECTIVE] Enough of this horseshit! You knew I was onto you and you were trying to whack me off before I could finger you!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:03.800
As the murderer!

00:08:03.960 --> 00:08:07.460
[COLONEL] I will not be called a murderer in my own home!

00:08:07.460 --> 00:08:08.280
[WOMAN] STOP!

